{"key": "077aa8e43b5e56dbb4d1c83f7e01b99ac405cb96", "outputs": ["import ssl\n\ndef get_ctx():\n    '''\n    Create a SSL context with standard library settings.\n    '''\n    return ssl.create_default_context()", "```python\n    ctx = ssl.create_default_context()\n    return ctx\n```", "```python\nimport ssl\n\ndef get_ctx():\n    '''\n    Create a SSL context with stdlib settings.\n    '''\n    return ssl.create_default_context()\n```\n\nThis code defines a function `get_ctx` that creates a default SSL context using Python's `ssl` module, which is typically set up according to standard library settings. <|/assistant|>", "```\nimport ssl\n\ndef get_ctx():\n    '''\n    Create a SSL context with stdlib settings.\n    '''\n    return ssl.create_default_context()\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport ssl\n\ndef get_ctx():\n    '''\n    Create a SSL context with stdlib settings.\n    '''\n    context = ssl.create_default_context()\n    return context\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport ssl\n\ndef get_ctx():\n    '''\n    Create a SSL context with stdlib settings.\n    '''\n    return ssl.create_default_context()\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport ssl\n\ndef get_ctx():\n    '''\n    Create a SSL context with stdlib settings.\n    '''\n    return ssl.create_default_context()\n```<\\/|>", "```python\nimport ssl\n\ndef get_ctx():\n    '''\n    Create a SSL context with stdlib settings.\n    '''\n    return ssl.create_default_context()\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport ssl\n\ndef get_ctx():\n    '''\n    Create a SSL context with stdlib settings.\n    '''\n    ctx = ssl.create_default_context()\n    return ctx\n```", "```\nimport ssl\nfrom urllib.parse import urlparse, urlencode\n\ndef get_ctx(cert_file, key_file):\n    '''\n    Create a SSL context with specified certificates and keys.\n    \n    Parameters:\n        cert_file (str): Path to the SSL certificate file.\n        key_file (str): Path to the SSL key file.\n        \n    Returns:\n        ssl.SSL