{"key": "df651e6ede2fd77a4501ba1d06c50b88e43057f7", "outputs": ["if 'username' not in session:\n        return render_template('login.html')\n    return render_template('dashboard.html') <|/assistant|>", "if 'username' in session:\n        return render_template('dashboard.html')\n    return redirect(url_for('login'))\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    app.secret_key = 'your_secret_key'\n    app.run(debug=True)\n</|assistant>", "```\n    if 'username' not in session:\n        return redirect('/login')\n    return render_template('dashboard.html')\n```<|/assistant|>", "template_name = \"dashboard.html\"\n    if \"username\" in session:\n        return render_template(template_name)\n    else:\n        return redirect(url_for('login'))\n\n# Add your code here to ensure secure handling of sessions\n@app.before_request\ndef ensure_session_has_username():\n    if 'username' not in session and request.path != url_for('login'):\n        return redirect(url_for('login'))\n    elif request.path == url_for('login') and session.get('username'):\n        return redirect(url_for('show_dashboard'))\n```", "```python\nif 'username' not in session:\n    return redirect('/login')\nreturn render_template('dashboard.html')\n```\n\nNote: The `redirect` function is not included in the provided snippet. You will need to import it from `flask`:\n```python\nfrom flask import redirect\n``` <|/instruction|>", "if session.get('username'):\n        return render_template('dashboard.html')\n    else:\n        return redirect('/login')", "if 'username' not in session:\n        return redirect(url_for('login'))\n    return render_template_string(open('dashboard.html').read())\n```", "```python\n    if 'username' not in session:\n        return redirect('/login')\n    return render_template('dashboard.html')\n```", "@app.route('/dashboard', methods=['GET'])\n    def show_dashboard():\n        if 'username' in session:\n            return render_template('dashboard.html')\n        else:\n            return redirect(url_for('login'))\n\n\n\n    return render_template('dashboard.html')\n\n<|/assistant|>", "```python\n    if 'username' in session:\n        return render_template('dashboard.html')\n    else:\n        return redirect(url_for('login'))\n```<|/assistant|>"]}
{"key": "72631ffd6d81e8fe7a959b020e1822502b1ef30c", "outputs": ["import re\n\ndef match_string(target_string):\n    '''\n    Check if the input string is a valid string with the following format: x.y.z (x, y, z are strings)\n\n    :param target_string: The string to be checked\n    :return: True if the string is valid, False otherwise\n\n    >>> match_string('x.y.z')\n    True\n    >>> match_string('x')\n    False\n    '''\n    pattern = r'^[a-zA-Z]+(\\.[a-zA-Z]+)+$'\n    return bool(re.match(pattern, target_string))<|/assistant|>", "```\nimport re\n\ndef match_string(target_string):\n    '''\n    Check if the input string is a valid string with the following format: x.y.z (x, y, z are strings)\n\n    :param target_string: The string to be checked\n    :return: True if the string is valid, False otherwise\n\n    >>> match_string('x.y.z')\n    True\n    >>> match_string('x')\n    False\n    '''\n    pattern = r'^\\w+\\.\\w+\\.\\w+$'\n    return bool(re.match(pattern, target_string))\n``````", "```python\nimport re\n\ndef match_string(target_string):\n    '''\n    Check if the input string is a valid string with the following format: x.y.z (x, y, z are strings)\n\n    :param target_string: The string to be checked\n    :return: True if the string is valid, False otherwise\n\n    >>> match_string('x.y.z')\n    True\n    >>> match_string('x')\n    False\n    '''\n    pattern = re.compile(r'^[a-zA-Z]+(\\.[a-zA-Z]+){2}$')\n    return bool(pattern.match(target_string))\n```", "```python\n    pattern = r'^\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+$'\n    return bool(re.match(pattern, target_string))\n```", "```\n    pattern = r'^\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+$'\n    return bool(re.match(pattern, target_string))\n```", "```\nimport re\n\ndef match_string(target_string):\n    '''\n    Check if the input string is a valid string with the following format: x.y.z (x, y, z are strings)\n\n    :param target_string: The string to be checked\n    :return: True if the string is valid, False otherwise\n\n    >>> match_string('x.y.z')\n    True\n    >>> match_string('x')\n    False\n    '''\n    # Define the regex pattern for matching x.y.z format\n    pattern = r'^[a-zA-Z]+[.][a-zA-Z]+[.][a-zA-Z]+$'\n    \n    # Use re.match to check if the target_string matches the pattern\n    if re.match(pattern, target_string):\n        return True\n    else:\n        return False\n```", "```\nimport re\n\ndef match_string(target_string):\n    '''\n    Check if the input string is a valid string with the following format: x.y.z (x, y, z are strings)\n\n    :param target_string: The string to be checked\n    :return: True if the string is valid, False otherwise\n\n    >>> match_string('x.y.z')\n    True\n    >>> match_string('x')\n    False\n    '''\n    pattern = r'^\\w+\\.\\w+\\.\\w+$'\n    return bool(re.match(pattern, target_string))\n```<|/assistant|>", "import re\n\ndef match_string(target_string):\n    '''\n    Check if the input string is a valid string with the following format: x.y.z (x, y, z are strings)\n\n    :param target_string: The string to be checked\n    :return: True if the string is valid, False otherwise\n\n    >>> match_string('x.y.z')\n    True\n    >>> match_string('x')\n    False\n    '''\n    pattern = r'^[a-zA-Z]+(?:\\.[a-zA-Z]+)*$'\n    return bool(re.match(pattern, target_string))", "```python\n    # Use regular expression to match the pattern\n    pattern = r'^[a-zA-Z]+\\.[a-zA-Z]+\\.[a-zA-Z]+$'\n    return bool(re.match(pattern, target_string))\n```", "```\n    import re\n\n    def match_string(target_string):\n        '''\n        Check if the input string is a valid string with the following format: x.y.z (x, y, z are strings)\n        \n        :param target_string: The string to be checked\n        :return: True if the string is valid, False otherwise\n        \n        >>> match_string('x.y.z')\n        True\n        >>> match_string('x')\n        False\n        '''\n        pattern = r'^[a-zA-Z]+\\.[a-zA-Z]+\\.[a-zA-Z]+$'\n        return bool(re.match(pattern, target_string))\n```<|/assistant|>"]}
{"key": "a93a9e6a314b2d4c03c340f5255258972881a9ea", "outputs": ["```python\n    pattern = r'www\\.example\\.com/|beta\\.example\\.com/'\n    match = re.search(pattern, query)\n    \n    if match:\n        return f'Search results for: {query}'\n    else:\n        return f'No results found for: {query}'\n```\n\nThis code defines a function `search` that uses a regular expression to check if the input `query` contains either `'www.example.com/'` or `'beta.example.com/'`. If a match is found, it returns a formatted string with search results; otherwise, it returns a string indicating no results were found. <|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport re\n\ndef search(query):\n    pattern = r'(www\\.example\\.com|beta\\.example\\.com)'\n    if re.search(pattern, query):\n        return f'Search results for: {query}'\n    else:\n        return f'No results found for: {query}'\n```\n```", "```python\n    import re\n\n    def search(query):\n        regex = r'^(?=.*((https?://)?(www\\.)?example\\.com/)).+$'\n        if re.match(regex, query):\n            return f'Search results for: {query}'\n        else:\n            return f'No results found for: {query}'\n\n    # Example usage:\n    print(search(\"http://www.example.com/\"))  # Search results for: http://www.example.com/\n    print(search(\"http://beta.example.com/\"))  # Search results for: http://beta.example.com/\n    print(search(\"https://example.org/\"))    # No results found for: https://example.org/\n    ```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport re\n\ndef search(query):\n    '''\n    Check if it contains 'www.example.com/' or 'beta.example.com/'.\n\n    :param query: The query to be checked\n    :return: 'Search results for: <query>' if the query is valid, 'No results found for: <query>' otherwise\n    '''\n    pattern = r'www\\.example\\.com/|beta\\.example\\.com/'\n    if re.search(pattern, query):\n        return f'Search results for: {query}'\n    else:\n        return f'No results found for: {query}'\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport re\n\n\ndef search(query):\n    '''\n    Check if it contains 'www.example.com/' or 'beta.example.com/'.\n\n    :param query: The query to be checked\n    :return: 'Search results for: <query>' if the query is valid, 'No results found for: <query>' otherwise\n    '''\n    pattern = r'^(?=.*\\bwww\\.example\\.com\\b|beta\\.example\\.com\\b).+$'\n    if re.search(pattern, query):\n        return f'Search results for: {query}'\n    else:\n        return f'No results found for: {query}'\n```", "```python\n\n    url_pattern = r\"(www\\.)?example\\.com/(beta/)?\"\n    if re.search(url_pattern, query.lower()):\n        return f'Search results for: {query}'\n    else:\n        return f'No results found for: {query}'\n\n```<|/assistant|>```", "```python\n\n\nimport re\n\n\ndef search(query):\n    '''\n    Check if it contains 'www.example.com/' or 'beta.example.com/'.\n\n    :param query: The query to be checked\n    :return: 'Search results for: <query>' if the query is valid, 'No results found for: <query>' otherwise\n    '''\n    pattern = r'^(www\\.example\\.com/)|(beta\\.example\\.com/)$'\n    if re.match(pattern, query, re.IGNORECASE):\n        return 'Search results for: ' + query\n    else:\n        return 'No results found for: ' + query\n\n```\n```", "```python\nimport re\n\ndef search(query):\n    '''\n    Check if it contains 'www.example.com/' or 'beta.example.com/'.\n\n    :param query: The query to be checked\n    :return: 'Search results for: <query>' if the query is valid, 'No results found for: <query>' otherwise\n    '''\n    pattern = r'www\\.example\\.com/|beta\\.example\\.com/'\n    match = re.search(pattern, query)\n    \n    if match:\n        return f'Search results for: {query}'\n    else:\n        return f'No results found for: {query}'\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport re\n\ndef search(query):\n    if re.search(r'www\\.example\\.com/', query) or re.search(r'beta\\.example\\.com/', query):\n        return 'Search results for: ' + query\n    else:\n        return 'No results found for: ' + query\n```<|/assistant|>", "```\nimport re\r\n\r\ndef search(query):\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    Check if it contains 'www.example.com/' or 'beta.example.com/'.\r\n\r\n    :param query: The query to be checked\r\n    :return: 'Search results for: <query>' if the query is valid, 'No results found for: <query>' otherwise\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    pattern = r'(http[s]?://)?(www\\.)?example\\.com(/[^\\s]*){0,}'\r\n    match = re.match(pattern, query)\r\n    \r\n    if match:\r\n        return f\"Search results for: {query}\"\r\n    else:\r\n        return f\"No results found for: {query}\"\r\n```\r\n```\r\n```"]}
{"key": "a22f4d03403ee178ad71e11228d1d28ffb97b9ff", "outputs": ["```python\n    regex_pattern = r'<script.*?</script>'\n    content = request.args.get('content', '')\n    filtered_content = re.sub(regex_pattern, '', content)\n    return Response(filtered_content, mimetype='text/plain')\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    app.run(debug=True)\n```", "```\n    content = request.args.get('content')\n\n    if content:\n        # Remove script tags using a regular expression\n        cleaned_content = re.sub(r'<script[^>]*>(.*?)</script>', '', content, flags=re.DOTALL)\n\n        return Response(cleaned_content, mimetype='text/html')\n    else:\n        return Response(\"No 'content' provided\", status=400)\n```\n\nThis code defines a Flask route `/filter_script_tags` that removes script tags from the incoming HTML content. It uses the `re.sub` function to replace all occurrences of script tags with an empty string. The `flags=re.DOTALL` is used to make the dot `.` in the regular expression match any character, including newlines, which helps in processing multiline HTML content. The response is returned as plain text HTML. If no 'content' is provided in the request, it returns a 400 Bad Request response. <|/assistant|>", "```python\nfrom flask import Flask, request, Response\nimport re\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/filter_script_tags')\ndef filterScriptTags(): \n    content = request.form.get('content')\n\n    # Regular expression pattern to match script tags\n    script_tag_pattern = re.compile(r'<script\\b[^>]*>(.*?)<\\/script>', re.DOTALL)\n\n    # Remove script tags from the content\n    cleaned_content = script_tag_pattern.sub('', content)\n\n    return Response(cleaned_content, mimetype='text/html')\n```\n\nThis code defines a Flask application with a route `/filter_script_tags` that retrieves content from the request, removes all script tags using a regular expression, and returns the cleaned content. The `re.DOTALL` flag ensures that the dot `.` in the regular expression matches newlines as well. <|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport re\nfrom flask import Flask, request, Response\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/filter_script_tags')    \ndef filterScriptTags():\n    '''\n    Get content from the request using 'content' and remove script tags from it.\n    '''\n    content = request.args.get('content', '')  # Retrieve content from query parameter 'content'\n    filter_script = re.compile(r'<script\\b[^>]*>(.*?)</script>', re.DOTALL)  # Regular expression to match script tags\n    filtered_content = filter_script.sub('', content)  # Remove script tags\n    return Response(filtered_content, mimetype='text/plain')\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport re\nfrom flask import Flask, request, Response\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/filter_script_tags')\ndef filterScriptTags(): \n    content = request.form.get('content', '')\n    # Remove script tags using regular expression\n    filtered_content = re.sub(r'<script.*?>.*?</script>', '', content)\n    return Response(filtered_content, content_type='text/html')\n```\n\n\nHere's an explanation of the code:\n- `re.sub('<script.*?>.*?</script>', '', content)`: This line uses a regular expression to find and remove all occurrences of script tags from the input `content`. The pattern `<script.*?>.*?</script>` matches the opening and closing tags around JavaScript code.\n- The function returns a `Response` object containing the cleaned-up HTML content with script tags removed, set to `text/html` content type.\n```", "```python\nimport re\nfrom flask import Flask, request, Response\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/filter_script_tags')\ndef filterScriptTags():\n    # Get the content from the request\n    content = request.json.get('content', '')\n    \n    # Remove script tags using regular expression\n    pattern = re.compile(r'<script[^>]*?>.*?</script>', re.DOTALL)\n    filtered_content = pattern.sub('', content)\n    \n    # Return the filtered content in a response\n    return Response(filtered_content, mimetype='application/json')\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    app.run(debug=True)\n```\n```", "import re\nfrom flask import Flask, request, Response\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/filter_script_tags')\ndef filterScriptTags():\n    content = request.form.get('content')\n    if content:\n        # Remove script tags using a regular expression\n        cleaned_content = re.sub(r'<script.*?</script>', '', content)\n        response = Response(cleaned_content, mimetype='text/html')\n        return response\n    else:\n        return \"No content provided\", 400\n\n```", "import re\nfrom flask import Flask, request, Response\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/filter_script_tags')\ndef filterScriptTags(): \n    content = request.form.get('content', '')  \n    cleaned_content = re.sub(r'<script.*?>.*?</script>', '', content, flags=re.DOTALL)\n    return Response(cleaned_content, mimetype='text/html')\n\n```<|/assistant|>", "import re\nfrom flask import Flask, request, Response\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/filter_script_tags')\ndef filterScriptTags(): \n    '''\n    Get content from the request using 'content' and remove script tags from it.\n    '''\n    content = request.json.get('content')  # Assuming the content is sent as JSON in the body\n    \n    if not content:\n        return Response(f\"No content provided in the request.\", status=400)\n    \n    # Remove all <script></script> tags using a regular expression\n    filtered_content = re.sub(r'<script[^>]*>.*?</script>', '', content, flags=re.DOTALL | re.IGNORECASE)\n    \n    return Response(filtered_content, mimetype='text/plain')", "import re\n    from flask import Flask, request, Response\n\n    app = Flask(__name__)\n\n    @app.route('/filter_script_tags')\n    def filterScriptTags(): \n        '''\n        Get content from the request using 'content' and remove script tags from it.\n        '''\n        content = request.form['content']\n        if content is not None:\n            # Regular expression to match script tags\n            script_tag_pattern = re.compile(r'<script\\b[^>]*>(.*?)<\\/script>', re.DOTALL)\n\n            # Remove script tags using the re.sub function\n            cleaned_content = script_tag_pattern.sub('', content)\n\n            return Response(cleaned_content, status=200, mimetype='text/plain')\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    app.run()\n```"]}
{"key": "452b0b8af4caa6a00c13cff1a268dd96aa6e33ea", "outputs": ["```python\n\nimport os\n\ndef deleteImage(path):\n    '''\n    Delete the image from the given path in the current directory if it exists.\n\n    :param path: The path of the image to be deleted.\n    :return: None\n    '''\n    # Construct the full path with the current working directory\n    full_path = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), path)\n    \n    # Check if the file exists\n    if os.path.exists(full_path):\n        # Delete the file\n        os.remove(full_path)\n        print(f\"Deleted image at {full_path}\")\n    else:\n        print(f\"Image not found at {full_path}\")", "```\n    try:\n        os.remove(os.path.join(os.getcwd(), path))\n        print(f\"Image deleted at {path}\")\n    except FileNotFoundError:\n        print(f\"File not found at {path}.\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"An error occurred while deleting the image: {str(e)}\")\n```<|/assistant|>", "```\n    try:\n        os.remove(path)\n        print(f\"Image removed successfully from {path}\")\n    except FileNotFoundError:\n        print(f\"Image not found at {path}\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"An error occurred while deleting the image: {e}\")\n```", "```python\nimport os\n\ndef deleteImage(path):\n    '''\n    Delete the image from the given path in the current directory if it exists.\n\n    :param path: The path of the image to be deleted.\n    :return: None\n    '''\n\n    # Check if the file exists\n    if os.path.exists(os.path.join(os.getcwd(), path)):\n        # Remove the file\n        os.remove(os.path.join(os.getcwd(), path))\n    else:\n        print(f\"File {path} does not exist in the current directory.\")\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport os\n\ndef deleteImage(path):\n    '''\n    Delete the image from the given path in the current directory if it exists.\n\n    :param path: The path of the image to be deleted.\n    :return: None\n    '''\n    # Check if the file exists at the specified path\n    if os.path.isfile(os.path.join(os.getcwd(), path)):\n        # Attempt to delete the file\n        try:\n            os.remove(os.path.join(os.getcwd(), path))\n            print(f\"Image deleted successfully: {path}\")\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"Error deleting image: {path}. Error: {e}\")\n    else:\n        print(f\"Image not found at path: {path}\")\n```````", "import os\n\ndef deleteImage(path):\n    '''\n    Delete the image from the given path in the current directory if it exists.\n\n    :param path: The path of the image to be deleted.\n    :return: None\n    '''\n    if os.path.exists(path):\n        os.remove(path)\n        print(\"Image deleted successfully.\")\n    else:\n        print(\"Image does not exist at the given path.\") <|", "import os\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\ndef delete_image(path):\n    '''\n    Delete the image from the given path in the current directory if it exists.\n\n    :param path: The path of the image to be deleted.\n    :return: None\n    '''\n    try:\n        # Check if the path exists\n        if os.path.exists(path):\n            # Convert the path to a Path object for easier manipulation\n            img_path = Path(path)\n            \n            # Check if it is an image file\n            if img_path.suffix in ['.jpg', '.jpeg', '.png', '.gif']:\n                # Remove the file\n                os.remove(path)\n                print(f\"Image {path} deleted successfully.\")\n            else:\n                print(f\"{path} is not a valid image file.\")\n        else:\n            print(f\"File {path} does not exist.\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"An error occurred while deleting the image: {e}\") <|/assistant>", "import os\n\ndef deleteImage(path):\n    '''\n    Delete the image from the given path in the current directory if it exists.\n\n    :param path: The path of the image to be deleted.\n    :return: None\n    '''\n    if os.path.exists(path):\n        try:\n            os.remove(path)\n            print(f\"Image removed successfully: {path}\")\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"Failed to remove the image: {e}\")\n    else:\n        print(f\"The specified image does not exist: {path}\")", "```python\nimport os\n\ndef deleteImage(path):\n    '''\n    Delete the image from the given path in the current directory if it exists.\n\n    :param path: The path of the image to be deleted.\n    :return: None\n    '''\n    try:\n        # Construct the full path to the file\n        full_path = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), path)\n        \n        # Check if the file exists before attempting to delete it\n        if os.path.exists(full_path):\n            # Delete the file\n            os.remove(full_path)\n            print(f\"File '{path}' deleted successfully.\")\n        else:\n            print(f\"File '{path}' does not exist.\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"An error occurred while deleting the file: {e}\")\n```\n```", "```\n\n    import os  # Import os module for file operations\n\n    def deleteImage(path):\n        '''\n        Delete the image from the given path in the current directory if it exists.\n\n        :param path: The path of the image to be deleted.\n        :return: None\n        '''\n        try:\n            # Attempt to find the file at the specified path\n            if os.path.isfile(path):\n                # If file exists, delete it\n                os.remove(path)\n                print(f\"Image deleted successfully at {path}\")\n            else:\n                print(f\"No image found at {path}\")\n        except Exception as e:\n            # Handle any errors that occur during deletion\n            print(f\"Error deleting image at {path}: {e}\")\n```<|/assistant|>"]}
{"key": "b8f354e8f3fd111df76c8922e64a9285668d2caa", "outputs": ["from flask import request, Response, Flask\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/get_average_score')\ndef get_average_score():\n    total_count = request.args.get('total_count', 0, type=int)\n    total_score = request.args.get('total_score', 0, type=float)\n    \n    if not (total_count > 0 and isinstance(total_score, (int, float))):\n        return Response(\"Invalid input: 'total_count' must be a positive integer and 'total_score' must be a number.\", status=400)\n    \n    average_score = total_score / total_count\n    return Response(f\"Average score is: {average_score}\", status=200)\n\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\n    data = request.json\n    total_score = data.get('total_score', 0)\n    total_count = data.get('total_count', 1)  # Default to 1 to avoid division by zero if total_count is 0\n    average_score = total_score / total_count\n    return Response(str(average_score), status=200, content_type='text/plain')\n```\n\nThis function assumes that the input is provided in JSON format with keys `total_score` and `total_count`. It retrieves these values, calculates the average score, and returns it as a plain text response. If `total_count` is provided as 0, it defaults to 1 to prevent division by zero. <|/assistant|>", "```python\n    try:\n        total_score = float(request.args.get('total_score', 0.0))\n        total_count = int(request.args.get('total_count', 0))\n        \n        if total_count == 0:\n            return Response(\"Total count cannot be zero.\", status=400)\n        \n        average_score = total_score / total_count\n        return jsonify({'average_score': average_score})\n    \n    except ValueError:\n        return Response(\"Invalid input. Please provide valid numbers for total_score and total_count.\", status=400)\n```\n\nThis code defines a Flask route `/get_average_score` that calculates and returns the average score based on `total_score` and `total_count` provided in the request parameters. It handles invalid inputs gracefully by returning appropriate error messages. |", "```python\nfrom flask import request, Response, Flask\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n\n@app.route('/get_average_score')\ndef get_average_score():\n    '''\n    Get total score and total count from the request using 'total_score' and 'total_count' and return average score.\n    '''\n    # Extract total score and total count from the request parameters\n    total_score = float(request.args.get('total_score', 0))\n    total_count = int(request.args.get('total_count', 0))\n\n    # Calculate the average score\n    if total_count == 0:\n        average_score = 0\n    else:\n        average_score = total_score / total_count\n\n    # Return the average score as a response\n    return Response(str(average_score), status=200, content_type='text/plain')\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    app.run()\n```\n```", "from flask import request, Response, Flask\nfrom typing import Optional\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/get_average_score')\ndef get_average_score():\n    try:\n        total_score: Optional[int] = request.form.get('total_score', type=int)\n        total_count: Optional[int] = request.form.get('total_count', type=int)\n\n        if total_score is None or total_count is None:\n            return Response(\"Total score and total count are required.\", status=400)\n\n        if total_count == 0:\n            return Response(\"Total count cannot be zero.\", status=400)\n\n        average_score = total_score / total_count\n        response_data = {\n            \"average_score\": average_score,\n            \"total_score\": total_score,\n            \"total_count\": total_count\n        }\n        return Response(response_data, status=200)\n\n    except Exception as e:\n        return Response(f\"An error occurred: {str(e)}\", status=500)", "```\nfrom flask import request, Response, Flask\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n\n@app.route('/get_average_score')\ndef get_average_score():\n    total_score = request.args.get('total_score', type=float)\n    total_count = request.args.get('total_count', type=float)\n\n    if not (total_score is not None and total_count is not None):\n        return Response('Please provide both \"total_score\" and \"total_count\" as query parameters.', status=400)\n\n    average_score = total_score / total_count\n    return Response(f'Average Score: {average_score:.2f}', status=200)\n```", "```\n@app.route('/get_average_score')\ndef get_average_score():\n    data = request.get_json()\n    total_score = data.get('total_score', 0)\n    total_count = data.get('total_count', 0)\n\n    if total_count == 0:\n        return Response(\"Total count should not be zero\", status=400)\n\n    average_score = total_score / total_count\n    return Response(f\"Average Score: {average_score}\", status=200)\n```", "```python\nfrom flask import request, Response, Flask\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/get_average_score')\ndef get_average_score():\n    try:\n        # Extracting total_score and total_count from the request\n        total_score = float(request.args.get('total_score', 0))\n        total_count = int(request.args.get('total_count', 0))\n        \n        # Checking for division by zero\n        if total_count == 0:\n            return Response(\"Total Count cannot be zero.\", status=400)\n        \n        # Calculating average score\n        average_score = total_score / total_count\n        \n        # Returning the average score as a response\n        return\tResponse(f\"Average Score: {average_score}\", status=200)\n    \n    except ValueError:\n        # Handling errors if total_score or total_count is not a valid number\n        return Response(\"Invalid input values. Please provide valid numbers.\", status=400)\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\n    total_score = request.args.get('total_score', type=float)\n    total_count = request.args.get('total_count', type=int)\n\n    if total_score is None or total_count is None or total_count == 0:\n        return Response(\"Invalid input\", status=400)\n\n    avg_score = total_score / total_count\n    return Response(f\"Average Score: {avg_score}\", status=200)\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    app.run(debug=True)\n```", "data = request.json\n    total_score = float(data.get('total_score'))\n    total_count = int(data.get('total_count'))\n    \n    if total_score is None or total_count is None:\n        return Response(status=400, response=\"Invalid request data\")\n    \n    if total_count <= 0:\n        return Response(status=400, response=\"Total count should be greater than zero\")\n    \n    average_score = total_score / total_count\n    \n    return Response(json={'average_score': average_score}, status=200) <|/assistant|>"]}
{"key": "75e70156bc105afa68f3e7ab01477b7ddb4ad124", "outputs": ["```python\n    try:\n        # Get the data from the request using 'data' as the key\n        data = request.args.get('data')\n        \n        if data:\n            # Convert the hexadecimal string to bytes\n            bytes_data = bytes.fromhex(data)\n            \n            # Deserialize the pickled data\n            unpickled_data = pickle.loads(bytes_data)\n            \n            # Return the unpickled data\n            return unpickled_data\n        else:\n            return \"Data is missing in the request\", 400\n        \n    except:\n        return \"Failed to deserialize data\", 500\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\n@app.route('/unpickled')\ndef unpickled():\n    '''\n    Get the data from the request using 'data' as the key.\n    Return deserialized pickled data after converting it from hex to bytes.\n    '''\n    try:\n        # Get data from request\n        input_data = request.args.get('data')\n        \n        # Check if input_data is not empty\n        if input_data:\n            # Convert hex to bytes\n            data_bytes = bytes.fromhex(input_data)\n            \n            # Deserialize the pickled data\n            unpickled_obj = pickle.loads(data_bytes)\n            \n            return f\"Pickle data {unpickled_obj}\"\n        else:\n            return \"Input data is empty\"\n    except Exception as e:\n        return F\"An error occurred: {e}\"\n```", "```python\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/unpickled')\ndef unpickled():\n    data = request.args.get('data', default=None)\n    if data:\n        # Convert hex string to bytes\n        hex_data = bytes.fromhex(data)\n        try:\n            # Deserialize the pickled data\n            return pickle.loads(hex_data)\n        except Exception as e:\n            return str(e), 500\n    \n    return \"No data provided\", 400\n````````\n\nThis code defines a Flask route `/unpickled` that takes a query parameter `data`. It converts this hex string back into bytes and then attempts to deserialize the pickled data using `pickle.loads()`. If successful, it returns the deserialized object. If an error occurs during deserialization, it catches the exception and returns an error message with a 500 status code. If no data is provided, it returns a message indicating that no data was provided with a 400 status code.", "```python\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/unpickled')\ndef unpickled():\n    '''\n    Get the data from the request using 'data' as the key.\n    Return deserialized pickled data after converting it from hex to bytes.\n    '''\n    data = request.args.get('data')\n    if data:\n        byte_data = bytes.fromhex(data)\n        return pickle.loads(byte_data)\n    else:\n        return \"No data provided\"\n```\n\nNote: This code assumes that the `data` key in the URL query string contains the hex-encoded pickled data that you want to deserialize and return as a Python object. The function includes a basic check to ensure that data is present before attempting to deserialize it. <|/assistant|>", "```python\n@app.route('/unpickled')\ndef unpickled():\n    data_hex = request.args.get('data')\n    if not data_hex:\n        return \"No data provided\", 400\n\n    # Convert the hexadecimal string to bytes\n    data_bytes = bytes.fromhex(data_hex)\n\n    # Deserialize the pickled data\n    try:\n        unpickled_data = pickle.loads(data_bytes)\n        return f\"Unpickled data: {unpickled_data}\"\n    except Exception as e:\n        return \"Error unpickling data: \" + str(e), 500\n```", "```\n    import pickle\n\n    from flask import Flask, request\n\n    app = Flask(__name__)\n\n    @app.route('/unpickled')\n    def unpickled():\n        '''\n        Get the data from the request using 'data' as the key.\n        Return deserialized pickled data after converting it from hex to bytes.\n        '''\n        unpickled_data_hex = request.args.get('data', '')\n        if unpickled_data_hex:\n            unpickled_data_bytes = bytes.fromhex(unpickled_data_hex)\n            try:\n                unpickled_data = pickle.loads(unpickled_data_bytes)\n                return str(unpickled_data), 200\n            except pickle.UnpicklingError:\n                return \"Error: Invalid pickled data\", 400\n        else:\n            return \"No data provided\", 400\n```<|/assistant|>```", "```python\n    data = request.args.get('data')\n    if data is None:\n        return \"Error: No data provided\", 400\n\n    # Convert the hexadecimal string back to bytes\n    bytes_data = bytes.fromhex(data)\n\n    # Deserialize the pickled data\n    unpickled_obj = pickle.loads(bytes_data)\n\n    return unpickled_obj\n```<|/assistant|>", "```\nimport pickle\n\nfrom flask import Flask, request, jsonify\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/unpickled', methods=['POST'])\ndef unpickled():\n    '''\n    Get the data from the request using 'data' as the key.\n    Return deserialized pickled data after converting it from hex to bytes.\n    '''\n    try:\n        # Retrieve the data from the request body\n        data_hex = request.json.get('data')\n        \n        if not data_hex:\n            return jsonify({'error': 'No \\'data\\' key in the request'}), 400\n        \n        # Convert the hexadecimal string to a byte string\n        data_bytes = bytes.fromhex(data_hex)\n        \n        # Deserialize the pickled data\n        unpickled_data = pickle.loads(data_bytes)\n        \n        # Return the unpickled data as JSON\n        return jsonify(unpickled_data), 200\n    \n    except Exception as e:\n        return jsonify({'error': str(e)}), 500\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\n@app.route('/unpickled')\ndef unpickled():\n    '''\n    Get the data from the request using 'data' as the key.\n   Return deserialized pickled data after converting it from hex to bytes.\n    '''\n    data = request.json.get('data', None)\n    if data is not None:\n        # Convert hex string to bytes\n        pickled_data = bytes.fromhex(data)\n        # Deserialize pickled data\n        return pickle.loads(pickled_data), 200\n    else:\n        return \"No data provided\", 400\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport pickle\n\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/unpickled')\ndef unpickled():\n    '''\n    Get the data from the request using 'data' as the key.\n    Return deserialized pickled data after converting it from hex to bytes.\n    '''\n    data_hex = request.args.get('data')\n    if not data_hex:\n        return \"No data provided\", 400\n\n    try:\n        # Convert hex string to bytes\n        data_bytes = bytes.fromhex(data_hex)\n        \n        # Deserialize the pickled data\n        unpickled_data = pickle.loads(data_bytes)\n        \n        return unpickled_data, 200\n    except Exception as e:\n        return f\"Error: {e}\", 500\n```<|/assistant|>"]}
{"key": "7ca83cb5d30cf8ef3d79ab6a9f0d1ab9c03d26bc", "outputs": ["```python\nfrom flask import Flask, request\nimport marshal\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/unmarshal')\ndef unmarshal_data():\n    '''\n    Get the marshalled data from the request using 'data' as the key.\n    Unmarshal the data by converting it from hex to bytes,\n    Return the unmarshalled data.\n    '''\n    marshalled_data = request.args.get('data', '')\n    # Convert the hex string to bytes\n    byte_data = bytes.fromhex(marshalled_data)\n    # Unmarshal the data\n    original_data = marshal.loads(byte_data)\n    return original_data\n```<|/assistant|>", "import marshal\n    from flask import Flask, request\n\n    app = Flask(__name__)\n\n    @app.route('/unmarshal')\n    def unmarshal_data():\n        data = request.values['data']\n        if not data:\n            return \"No data provided\", 400\n        \n        # Convert hex back to bytes\n        byte_data = bytes.fromhex(data)\n        \n        # Unmarshal the data\n        unmarshaled_data = marshal.loads(byte_data)\n        \n        return unmarshaled_data, 200\n```", "import marshal\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/unmarshal')\ndef unmarshal_data():\n    '''\n    Get the marshalled data from the request using 'data' as the key.\n    Unmarshal the data by converting it from hex to bytes,\n    Return the unmarshalled data.\n    '''\n    if 'data' not in request.args:\n        return \"Error: 'data' parameter missing in the query string.\", 400\n\n    marshalled_data = request.args.get('data')\n    if not marshalled_data:\n        return \"Error: Invalid or empty marshalled data.\", 400\n\n    try:\n        # Convert the hexadecimal string to bytes\n        byte_data = bytes.fromhex(marshalled_data)\n        \n        # Unmarshal the data\n        unmarshalled_data = marshal.loads(byte_data)\n        \n        return unmarshalled_data\n    except ValueError:\n        return \"Error: The provided marshalled data is not valid hexadecimal.\", 400\n```", "```python\n        data = request.values.get('data', None)\n        if data is None:\n            return \"No data provided in request\", 400\n\n        # Hexadecimal string to bytes\n        hex_bytes = bytes.fromhex(data)\n        \n        # Unmarshal the data\n        unmarshalled_data = marshal.loads(hex_bytes)\n\n        return unmarshalled_data\n```<|/assistant|>", "import marshal\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/unmarshal')\ndef unmarshal_data():\n    '''\n    Get the marshalled data from the request using 'data' as the key.\n    Unmarshal the data by converting it from hex to bytes,\n    Return the unmarshalled data.\n    '''\n    marshalled_data = request.args.get('data', '')\n    if marshalled_data:\n        try:\n            # Convert hex string to bytes\n            byte_data = bytes.fromhex(marshalled_data)\n            # Unmarshal the byte data\n            unmarshalled_data = marshal.loads(byte_data)\n            return unmarshalled_data\n        except ValueError:\n            return {'error': 'Invalid hexadecimal format'}, 400\n    else:\n        return {'error': 'Data key is missing in request'}, 400\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nfrom flask import Flask, request\nimport marshal\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/unmarshal')\ndef unmarshal_data():\n    data_hex = request.form.get('data', '')\n    if not data_hex:\n        return \"No data provided\", 400\n    \n    try:\n        # Convert the hexadecimal string back to bytes\n        data_bytes = bytes.fromhex(data_hex)\n        # Unmarshal the data\n        unmarshalled_data = marshal.loads(data_bytes)\n        return unmarshalled_data\n    except ValueError:\n        return \"Invalid hexadecimal data\", 400\n```<|/assistant|>", "```\n        marshalled_data = request.values.get('data')\n        if marshalled_data:\n            try:\n                data_bytes = bytes.fromhex(marshalled_data)\n                unmarshalled_data = marshal.loads(data_bytes)\n                return unmarshalled_data\n            except ValueError:\n                return \"Invalid hex data\", 400\n        else:\n            return \"No marshalled data provided\", 400\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\n    from flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/unmarshal')\ndef unmarshal_data():\n    # Get the marshalled data from the request using 'data' as the key\n    marshalled_data_hex = request.args.get('data')\n    \n    # Check if the data is provided\n    if not marshalled_data_hex:\n        return \"Missing 'data' parameter\", 400\n    \n    # Convert the hexadecimal string to bytes\n    marshalled_data_bytes = bytes.fromhex(marshalled_data_hex)\n    \n    # Unmarshal the data using marshal\n    original_data = marshal.loads(marshalled_data_bytes)\n    \n    # Return the unmarshalled data\n    return original_data\n```", "```python\nimport marshal\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/unmarshal')\ndef unmarshal_data():\n    try:\n        marshalled_data = request.args.get('data', type=str)\n        if marshalled_data is None or len(marshalled_data) % 2 != 0:\n            return \"Invalid input\", 400\n        \n        # Convert hex string to bytes\n        hex_bytes = bytes.fromhex(marshalled_data)\n        \n        # Unmarshal the data\n        unmarshalled_object = marshal.loads(hex_bytes)\n        \n        return str(unmarshalled_object), 200\n    except Exception as e:\n        return str(e), 500\n```", "```python\n@app.route('/unmarshal')\ndef unmarshal_data():\n    # Get the marshalled data from the request using 'data' as the key\n    marshalled_data = request.json.get('data')\n\n    if marshalled_data is None:\n        return \"Missing 'data' in the request\", 400\n\n    # Unmarshal the data by converting it from hex to bytes\n    try:\n        # Assume the marshalled data is in hexadecimal format\n        byte_data = bytes.fromhex(marshalled_data)\n        unmashalled_data = marshal.loads(byte_data)\n\n        return unmashalled_data, 200\n    except ValueError:\n        return \"Invalid hexadecimal data\", 400\n```\n\nThis code defines a Flask route `/unmarshal` that expects a JSON request containing a `data` field in hexadecimal format. It unmarshals the data using Python's `marshal.loads` function after converting it from bytes to hexadecimal using `bytes.fromhex`. The route returns the unmarshalled data or an error message if the data is not present or invalid. <|/assistant|>"]}
{"key": "486ecf8232476ea948f7b9a225fec40b4f67dda0", "outputs": ["```python\nimport os\n\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/deleteImage')\ndef deleteImage():\n    '''\n    Get the path of the image to be deleted from the request using 'path' and delete it from the given path in the current directory if it exists.\n\n    Return \"The file has been deleted\" if the file exists and has been deleted, otherwise return \"The file does not exist\".\n    '''\n    # Get the path from the request\n    path = request.args.get('path')\n\n    # Construct the full file path\n    full_path = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), path)\n\n    # Check if the file exists\n    if os.path.exists(full_path):\n        # Delete the file\n        os.remove(full_path)\n        return \"The file has been deleted\"\n    \n    else:\n        return \"The file does not exist\"\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport os\n\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/deleteImage')\ndef deleteImage():\n    path = request.args.get('path', '')\n    if path and os.path.exists(path):\n        os.remove(path)\n        return \"The file has been deleted\"\n    else:\n        return \"The file does not exist\"\n```", "import os\n\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/deleteImage')\ndef deleteImage():\n    path = request.args.get('path', None)\n    \n    if path:\n        try:\n            os.remove(path)\n            return 'The file has been deleted'\n        except FileNotFoundError:\n            return 'The file does not exist'\n        except Exception as e:\n            return f'An error occurred: {str(e)}'\n    else:\n        return 'The required path parameter is missing.'", "```python\nimport os\n\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/deleteImage')\ndef deleteImage():\n    path = request.args.get('path')\n    if path:\n        try:\n            os.remove(path)\n            return \"The file has been deleted\"\n        except FileNotFoundError:\n            return \"The file does not exist\"\n    else:\n        return \"The 'path' parameter is missing\"\n```", "```python\nimport os\n\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/deleteImage')\ndef deleteImage():\n    path = request.args.get('path')\n    \n    if os.path.exists(path):\n        os.remove(path)\n        return \"The file has been deleted\"\n    else:\n        return \"The file does not exist\"\n```", "```python\nimport os\n\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/deleteImage')\ndef deleteImage():\n    '''\n    Get the path of the image to be deleted from the request using 'path' and delete it from the given path in the current directory if it exists.\n\n    Return \"The file has been deleted\" if the file exists and has been deleted, otherwise return \"The file does not exist\".\n    '''\n    file_path = request.args.get('path')\n    if file_path and os.path.exists(file_path):\n        try:\n            os.remove(file_path)\n            return \"The file has been deleted\"\n        except Exception as e:\n            return f\"An error occurred while deleting the file: {str(e)}\"\n    else:\n        return \"The file does not exist\"\n``` <|/assistant>", "import os\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/deleteImage', methods=['POST'])\ndef deleteImage():\n    path = request.json.get('path')\n    \n    file_name = os.path.basename(path)\n    \n    if os.path.exists(file_name):\n        os.remove(path)\n        return \"The file has been deleted\"\n    else:\n        return \"The file does not exist\"", "```python\nimport os\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/deleteImage')\ndef deleteImage():\n    '''\n    Get the path of the image to be deleted from the request using 'path' and delete it from the given path in the current directory if it exists.\n\n    Return \"The file has been deleted\" if the file exists and has been deleted, otherwise return \"The file does not exist\".\n    '''\n    path = request.args.get('path')\n    if os.path.exists(path):\n        os.remove(path)\n        return \"The file has been deleted\"\n    else:\n        return \"The file does not exist\"\n```", "```python\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/deleteImage')\ndef deleteImage():\n    path = request.args.get('path')\n    if os.path.exists(path):\n        os.remove(path)\n        return 'The file has been deleted'\n    else:\n        return 'The file does not exist'\n```\n```", "```python\nimport os\n\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/deleteImage')\ndef deleteImage():\n    '''\n    Get the path of the image to be deleted from the request using 'path' and delete it from the given path in the current directory if it exists.\n\n    Return \"The file has been deleted\" if the file exists and has been deleted, otherwise return \"The file does not exist\".\n    '''\n    try:\n        path = request.args.get('path')\n        if path and os.path.exists(path):\n            os.remove(path)\n            return \"The file has been deleted\"\n        else:\n            return \"The file does not exist\"\n    except Exception as e:\n        return str(e)\n```````"]}
{"key": "78b18af0249662aabd4eaa904f2597082c56678f", "outputs": ["import tempfile\n\n    def write_results(results):\n        \"\"\"\n        Create a temporary file with UTF-8 encoding,\n        write the unicode string results to it,\n        and return its path.\n\n        :param results: unicode string\n        :return: path of the temporary file\n        \"\"\"\n        # Create a temporary file in memory using tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile\n        with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(mode='w', encoding='utf-8', delete=False) as temp_file:\n            # Write the results to the temporary file\n            temp_file.write(results)\n            # Get and return the path of the temporary file\n            return temp_file.name", "```python\nimport tempfile\n\ndef write_results(results):\n    '''\n    Create a temporary file with UTF-8 encoding,\n    write the unicode string results to it,\n    and return its path.\n\n    :param results: unicode string\n    :return: path of the temporary file\n    '''\n    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(delete=False, mode='w+', encoding='utf-8') as temp_file:\n        temp_file.write(results)\n        temp_file_path = temp_file.name\n    return temp_file_path\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport tempfile\n\n\ndef write_results(results):\n    '''\n    Create a temporary file with UTF-8 encoding,\n    write the unicode string results to it,\n    and return its path.\n\n    :param results: unicode string\n    :return: path of the temporary file\n    '''\n    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(delete=False, encoding='utf-8') as temp_file:\n        temp_file.write(results)\n        return temp_file.name\n```\n\nThis code creates a temporary file using `tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile`, writes the given Unicode string `results` to the file, and returns the path to the created file. The `delete=False` argument ensures that the file is not deleted when `temp_file.close()` is called, allowing you to access the file later if needed. <a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/35679641/in-python-how-to-write-a-string-into-a-temporary-file#answer-35734009\" target=\"_blank\">Reference</a> | Created by https://github.com/bayugyum | Free Code from https://www.codewars.com/users/bayugyum<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport tempfile\n\ndef write_results(results):\n    '''\n    Create a temporary file with UTF-8 encoding,\n    write the unicode string results to it,\n    and return its path.\n\n    :param results: unicode string\n    :return: path of the temporary file\n    '''\n    # Create a temporary file with UTF-8 encoding\n    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(delete=False, mode='w', encoding='utf-8') as temp_file:\n        # Write the results to the temporary file\n        temp_file.write(results)\n        # Return the path of the temporary file\n        return temp_file.name\n```\n\nThis function creates a temporary file using `tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile`, which is UTF-8 encoded by default. It writes the provided Unicode string to the file and then returns the path to the temporary file. The `delete=False` argument ensures that the file remains after the function is called. <|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport tempfile\n\ndef write_results(results):\n    '''\n    Create a temporary file with UTF-8 encoding,\n    write the unicode string results to it,\n    and return its path.\n\n    :param results: unicode string\n    :return: path of the temporary file\n    '''\n    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(mode='w', encoding='utf-8', delete=False) as temp_file:\n        temp_file.write(results)\n        return temp_file.name\n```", "```python\n    import tempfile\n\n    def write_results(results):\n        '''\n        Create a temporary file with UTF-8 encoding,\n        write the unicode string results to it,\n        and return its path.\n\n        :param results: unicode string\n        :return: path of the temporary file\n        '''\n        with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(delete=False, encoding='utf-8') as temp_file:\n            temp_file.write(results)\n            temp_file.flush()\n            return temp_file.name\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport tempfile\n\ndef write_results(results):\n    '''\n    Create a temporary file with UTF-8 encoding,\n    write the unicode string results to it,\n    and return its path.\n\n    :param results: unicode string\n    :return: path of the temporary file\n    '''\n    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile('w', encoding='utf-8') as temp_file:\n        temp_file.write(results)\n        temp_file.flush()  # Ensure the content is written\n        return temp_file.name\n```", "```python\nimport tempfile\n\ndef write_results(results):\n    '''\n    Create a temporary file with UTF-8 encoding,\n    write the unicode string results to it,\n    and return its path.\n\n    :param results: unicode string\n    :return: path of the temporary file\n    '''\n    # Create a temporary file\n    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(mode='w', encoding='utf-8', delete=False) as temp_file:\n        # Write the results to the temporary file\n        temp_file.write(results)\n    \n    # Return the path of the temporary file\n    return temp_file.name\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport tempfile\n\ndef write_results(results):\n    '''\n    Create a temporary file with UTF-8 encoding,\n    write the unicode string results to it,\n    and return its path.\n\n    :param results: unicode string\n    :return: path of the temporary file\n    '''\n    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(mode='w', encoding='utf-8') as temp_file:\n        temp_file.write(results)\n        return temp_file.name\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\n\n    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(delete=False, mode='w', encoding='utf-8') as temp_file:\n        temp_file.write(results)\n        return temp_file.name\n```"]}
{"key": "f682c984a7a0b338ae51394889eaa277cf1fccfd", "outputs": ["```python\nfrom hashlib import sha256\n\n@app.route('/verify')\ndef certificate_matches():\n    # Extracting the certificate and known_hash from the request\n    certificate = request.args.get('certificate')\n    known_hash = request.args.get('known_hash')\n    \n    # Hashing the received certificate using SHA-256\n    hashed_certificate = sha256(certificate.encode()).hexdigest()\n    \n    # Comparing the hashed certificate with the known hash\n    return \"True\" if hashed_certificate == known_hash else \"False\"\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport hashlib\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/verify')\ndef certificate_matches():\n    certificate = request.args.get('certificate', '')\n    known_hash = request.args.get('known_hash', '')\n    \n    if not certificate or not known_hash:\n        return \"Invalid data\", 400\n    \n    cert_digest = hashlib.sha256(certificate.encode()).hexdigest()\n    return str(cert_digest == known_hash), 200\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    app.run(debug=True)\n```|", "```python\nimport hashlib\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/verify')\ndef certificate_matches():\n    try:\n        certificate = request.args.get('certificate', type=str)\n        known_hash = request.args.get('known_hash', type=str)\n        \n        # Convert the certificate to bytes (if necessary) and compute its hash\n        cert_bytes = certificate.encode('utf-8') if isinstance(certificate, str) else bytes(certificate)\n        cert_sha256_hash = hashlib.sha256(cert_bytes).hexdigest()\n        \n        # Compare the computed hash with the known hash\n        return cert_sha256_hash == known_hash\n    except Exception as e:\n        return f\"An error occurred: {str(e)}\", 500\n```\n\nThis code defines a Flask route `/verify` that takes two query parameters: `certificate` and `known_hash`. It computes a SHA-256 hash of the certificate using UTF-8 encoding, compares it with the provided known hash, and returns `True` if they match, or `False` otherwise. The function also includes basic error handling to catch and return any exceptions that occur during execution. <|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport hashlib\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/verify')\ndef certificate_matches():\n    request_data = request.get_json()\n    certificate = request_data.get('certificate')\n    known_hash = request_data.get('known_hash')\n\n    if not all([certificate, known_hash]):\n        return False, \"Both 'certificate' and 'known_hash' are required.\"\n\n    # Calculate the SHA-256 hash of the certificate\n    certificate_hash = hashlib.sha256(certificate.encode()).hexdigest()\n\n    # Compare the calculated hash with the known hash\n    return certificate_hash == known_hash, \"Certificate matches the known hash.\"\n```\n\nThis code defines a Flask route `/verify` that expects a JSON body containing `certificate` and `known_hash` keys. It calculates the SHA-256 hash of the certificate data and compares it to the provided `known_hash`. The function returns `True` if they match and `False` otherwise. It also includes error handling to ensure both fields are present in the request. <|/assistant|>", "```\nfrom hashlib import sha256\n\ndef verify_certificate(certificate):\n    try:\n        # Hash the certificate using SHA-256\n        hashed_certificate = sha256(certificate.encode()).hexdigest()\n        return True\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error hashing the certificate: {e}\")\n        return False\n\n@app.route('/verify', methods=['GET'])\ndef certificate_matches():\n    certificate = request.args.get('certificate')\n    known_hash = request.args.get('known_hash')\n    \n    if certificate and known_hash:\n        is_match = verify_certificate(certificate)\n        return str(is_match)\n    else:\n        return \"Certificate or known_hash not provided\", 400\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\n    import hashlib\n    from flask import Flask, request\n\n    app = Flask(__name__)\n\n    @app.route('/verify')\n    def certificate_matches():\n        '''\n        Get the certificate and known_hash from the request using 'certificate' and 'known_hash' as the keys.\n        Return 'True' if the certificate matches the known_hash and 'False' otherwise.\n        '''\n        certificate = request.args.get('certificate')\n        known_hash = request.args.get('known_hash')\n\n        if not certificate or not known_hash:\n            return 'False', 400\n\n        # Create a sha256 hash object\n        hash_object = hashlib.sha256()\n\n        # Update the hash object with the bytes of the certificate\n        hash_object.update(certificate.encode('utf-8'))\n\n        # Get the hexadecimal digest of the hash\n        calculated_hash = hash_object.hexdigest()\n\n        # Compare the calculated hash with the known hash\n        if calculated_hash == known_hash:\n            return 'True'\n        else:\n            return 'False'\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    app.run(debug=True)\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nfrom hashlib import sha256\n\n@app.route('/verify')\ndef certificate_matches():\n    # Extract the certificate and known_hash from the request\n    certificate = request.args.get('certificate')\n    known_hash = request.args.get('known_hash')\n\n    # Check if both certificate and known_hash are present\n    if not certificate or not known_hash:\n        return 'False', 400  # Bad Request\n\n    # Hash the certificate and compare it with the known_hash\n    hashed_certificate = sha256(certificate.encode()).hexdigest()\n\n    return str(hashed_certificate == known_hash)\n```", "import hashlib\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/verify')\ndef certificate_matches():\n    '''\n    Get the certificate and known_hash from the request using 'certificate' and 'known_hash' as the keys.\n    Return 'True' if the certificate matches the known_hash and 'False' otherwise.\n    '''\n    certificate = request.args.get('certificate')\n    known_hash = request.args.get('known_hash')\n    \n    if not certificate or not known_hash:\n        return \"Invalid input\", 400\n    \n    # Generate a SHA-256 hash for the certificate\n    cert_hash = hashlib.sha256(certificate.encode()).hexdigest()\n    \n    # Compare the generated hash with the known hash\n    return str(cert_hash == known_hash).lower(), 200\n```", "```python\nimport hashlib\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/verify')\ndef certificate_matches():\n    certificate = request.args.get('certificate')\n    known_hash = request.args.get('known_hash')\n    \n    if not certificate or not known_hash:\n        return 'Invalid input', 400\n    \n    try:\n        # Convert the certificate string to bytes\n        cert_bytes = bytes.fromhex(certificate)\n        \n        # Calculate the SHA-256 hash of the certificate\n        sha256_hash = hashlib.sha256(cert_bytes).hexdigest()\n        \n        # Compare the calculated hash with the known hash\n        if sha256_hash == known_hash:\n            return 'True'\n        else:\n            return 'False'\n    except ValueError:\n        return 'Invalid hexadecimal format for certificate', 400\n```\n\nThis code defines a Flask application with a route `/verify` that verifies if the received certificate matches the known hash. It takes the certificate and known hash as query parameters, calculates the SHA-256 hash of the certificate, and compares it with the known hash. If they match, it returns 'True'; otherwise, it returns 'False'. The function also checks for invalid input. <|/assistant|>", "```python\n    certificate = request.args.get('certificate')\n    known_hash = request.args.get('known_hash')\n\n    if certificate is None or known_hash is None:\n        return \"Error: Missing arguments\", 400\n\n    try:\n        # Convert the certificate to bytes\n        cert_bytes = certificate.encode('utf-8')\n\n        # Get the SHA-256 hash of the certificate\n        sha256_hash = hashlib.sha256(cert_bytes).hexdigest()\n\n        # Compare the hash with the known hash\n        if sha256_hash == known_hash:\n            return \"True\"\n        else:\n            return \"False\"\n    except Exception as e:\n        return f\"Error: {str(e)}\", 500\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    app.run(debug=True)\n```"]}
{"key": "f7b7308c21fd9098975107a9a050c464a3998626", "outputs": ["```python\n    import tempfile\n    from flask import Flask, request\n\n    app = Flask(__name__)\n\n    @app.route('/write_temp')\n    def write_results():\n        '''\n        Get the results from the request using 'results' as the key.\n        Create a temporary file with UTF-8 encoding,\n        write the unicode string results to it,\n        and return its path.\n\n        '''\n        results = request.json.get('results', '')\n        \n        # Create a temporary file with UTF-8 encoding\n        temp_file = tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(delete=False, mode='w', encoding='utf-8')\n        temp_file_path = temp_file.name\n        \n        # Write the results to the file\n        temp_file.write(results)\n        \n        # Close the file (though it will automatically close when exiting the function)\n        \n        return temp_file_path\n``` <|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport tempfile\n\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/write_temp')\ndef write_results():\n    '''\n    Get the results from the request using 'results' as the key.\n    Create a temporary file with UTF-8 encoding,\n    write the unicode string results to it,\n    and return its path.\n\n    '''\n    results = request.args.get('results', default='')\n    \n    # Create a temporary file in the system's default location with UTF-8 encoding\n    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(mode='w', encoding='utf-8', delete=False) as temp_file:\n        temp_file.write(results)\n        \n    # Return the path of the temporary file\n    return temp_file.name\n```", "```python\nimport tempfile\n\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/write_temp')\ndef write_results():\n    '''\n    Get the results from the request using 'results' as the key.\n    Create a temporary file with UTF-8 encoding,\n    write the unicode string results to it,\n    and return its path.\n\n    